;;; A disjunction nested inside a conjunction, in a hypothesis rule: `ein saturate`
;;; answers and every solve question stops — regression
;;; `nested-or-hrule`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A hypothesis rule is compiled by the pass that writes a state's `open` facts,
;;; never by a saturation.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; An `(or …)` is a whole `:match`, a hypothesis rule's as a rule's, so `h` is
;;; refused at load: every command exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `864b16ed`, release: `ein saturate` answered root's fixpoint, exit 0;
;;; `ein solve` (every mode), `oracle` and `render lattice` stopped, exit 1,
;;; on the compiler's line. The engine refuses it at load.

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(a k)
(rule h ()
  :match  (and (a ?x) (or (p ?x) (q ?x)))
  :assert (open (p ?x))
  :why "{?x} is an a, and a p or a q, so guess it is a p")
